#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Compression arc session B (notes/adr/0144-roadmap-row-contract.md).

Run ONCE, on 2026-08-17, to re-section `.agents/plans/roadmap.md` onto
the row contract author rulings Q1-Q5 ("a. throughout") define, and
which `ehrt.docs-tooling.roadmap-lint-test` gates:

    - <TOKEN> **[slug]** [PRIORITY n] <what remains and why> <ADR cite>

  TOKEN is `OPEN` | `CLOSED <yyyy-mm-dd> <ADR-NNNN|sha>` |
  `DEFERRED (trigger: ...)` | `EXTERNAL`; `CLOSED` only under `## Done`;
  `PRIORITY n` on `## Next` rows, unique and ascending; six lines max.

`roadmap.md` is hand-owned intent, so unlike `notes/ADRs.md` (ADR-0143)
it cannot be GENERATED. The judgement -- which token a row takes, which
clause of it survives, where the rest belongs -- is authored, in ROWS
below. What is mechanical, and what this script does, is the move:

  1. Every row leaves `roadmap.md` VERBATIM, into exactly one
     destination:
       * `attic`   -> `.agents/plans/roadmap-done-2026-08.md`, under one
                      dated `## ` header. Every CLOSED row goes here;
                      so does a live row with no owning ADR (Q4's own
                      fallback).
       * `adr:NNNN`-> `notes/adr/NNNN-*.md`, appended under
                      `### Roadmap history (moved verbatim from
                      roadmap.md by ADR-0144, 2026-08-17)`. This is the
                      only append these otherwise append-only files get
                      here; no pre-existing sentence is edited by this
                      script.
       * `None`    -> the row was already inside the six-line cap, so
                      nothing overflows: its rewrite is a reformat and
                      the commit diff is its own record.

  2. The row's replacement text (`new`, authored, `None` for a row that
     leaves the file) is written in its place.

  3. Every `## Done` pointer is retokened mechanically
     (`- DATE - slug - ADR` becomes `- CLOSED DATE ADR **[slug]**`), and
     the six Done lines the census found MISSING are inserted in date
     order (ADR-0126/0127/0128/0129/0132/0133 -- their rows had been
     carried in `## Next` as closed prose instead).

NOTHING-LOST PROOF, and why it is a multiset and not a diffstat. The
new rows are AUTHORED, not excerpted, so "the overflow" has no clean
line boundary to subtract. So each moved row goes to its destination
WHOLE, and the script asserts that the multiset of row lines removed
from `roadmap.md` equals, exactly, the multiset of lines added to the
destinations -- byte-identical, per line, per row. Scaffolding (dated
headers, blank separators) and the authored replacement rows are
counted and reported SEPARATELY, never netted against the proof.
`--dry-run` prints the whole ledger and writes nothing.

Idempotent by refusal: the script asserts each row's own first line
still matches what the census read at `deb9a33`, so a second run (or a
drifted tree) fails loud rather than double-appending.

Usage:  bin/roadmap-migrate-0144 [--dry-run] [--census] [--markdown] [--verify]

`--verify` re-reads the roadmap AS IT WAS at `deb9a33` and asserts that
every moved row's exact contiguous block is present in the destination
file NOW. This is the durable proof, re-runnable at any later commit,
and it is stronger than a diffstat: `git diff --numstat` UNDERCOUNTS a
move by however many moved lines its own alignment happens to render as
context rather than insertions (here, five).

`--markdown` emits the per-row disposition table ADR-0144 carries, from
this same table, so the ADR's census and the migration cannot disagree.
"""

import os
import re
import sys
from collections import Counter

ROADMAP = ".agents/plans/roadmap.md"
